hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18146","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Urwah ibn Muhammad ibn Atiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The giving hand is better than the lower hand."
"18147","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Shibl and others narrated to me, from Urwah ibn Muhammad who said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the ruler rages, Satan gains mastery."
"18148","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Wail Sanani Muradi narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with Urwah ibn Muhammad, when a man was brought in to him and spoke to him with words that angered him. When he became angry, he stood up, then returned to us having performed ablution, and said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather Atiyyah, who had companionship, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire, and fire is only extinguished with water; so if one of you becomes angry, let him perform ablution."
